      "doctor_question": "Hello. What brings you into the clinic today?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S019",
      "patient_response": "I'm here because people keep acting like I'm imagining it, but I know the hospital people and some folks from the agency have been watching our house and my cleaning routes to see if I'm taking proper care of my husband. It's just like when I was working at that big house out on Elm Street, you know, the one with the huge oak tree in the front yard? The lady there, Mrs. Higgins, she always thought I wasn't dusting the baseboards right, and she'd follow me around with a white glove. Can you believe that? A white glove in this day and age! Anyway, my husband likes his dinner exactly at 6:00 PM, and if I'm late because I'm trying to dodge these people watching me, he gets so cranky. He used to work at the auto plant before his back gave out. They made good cars back then, not like the plastic things they sell now. I used to have a Chevy Nova, cherry red. Loved that car. But yeah, they're definitely watching me, taking notes on how I do things.",
