    {
      "turn": 2,
      "doctor_question": "Have you ever heard people talking or heard any sounds that others around you couldn't hear?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S020",
      "patient_response": "Well, yes, actually. Even when the house is completely quiet, I'll hear this woman's voice. It usually comes from right near the kitchen window, and it's as clear as if she were standing right next to me. She tells me to go check the locks or move my husband's pills around. Speaking of pills, he takes so many now, it's like a whole pharmacy on the counter. The little orange ones are for his blood pressure, I think. We used to go to that pharmacy on Main Street, the one with the soda fountain? Oh, they had the best cherry phosphates. You just don't see soda fountains anymore. Everything is big chain stores now, all bright lights and self-checkout machines that never work right. \"Unexpected item in the bagging area,\" it always says. Drives me up the wall. But yes, that woman's voice, it's very clear. I always check the window, but nobody's there.",
