      "doctor_question": "Aside from the stress of feeling watched, how has your mood been lately—have you been feeling consistently down, sad, or depressed?",
      "targeted_symptom": null,
      "patient_response": "Down? No, I wouldn't say I've been feeling sad. I really don't have the time to sit around feeling depressed, not with all the work I have to get done. Just yesterday I was scrubbing the grout in the master bathroom over at the Miller's house—they have this beautiful white subway tile, you know? But grout is just a complete nightmare to keep clean. I tried one of those new bleach pens they advertise on TV. Have you seen those commercials? The ones with the little animated scrubbing bubbles? I always loved those commercials when I was younger. My brother used to try and draw them on his school folders. He was such a good artist, he actually won a blue ribbon at the county fair back in, oh, it must have been '82, for a charcoal drawing of a horse. A palomino, I think it was. Beautiful animals, horses. I always wanted to ride one but my husband is terribly allergic to hay, so we never went near the stables. But anyway, no, my mood is fine, I'm not sad. Just busy trying to keep everything clean before they write it down.",
